<title>SINGAPORE: Hour Glass 1996/97 net falls 25.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Hour Glass 1996/97 net falls 25.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    8.6  vs    11.7</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (cts)		2.5  vs     3.125</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		   7.98 vs    10.76</p>
<p>    Group share fully dil (cts)     7.87 vs    10.66</p>
<p>    Turnover			    413.25 vs   434.43</p>
<p>    Other income			  0.83 vs     1.16</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    1.61 vs     2.10</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	 4.53 vs     4.72</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		   5.33 vs	nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     14.27 vs    18.15</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    0.16 vs     0.11 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				     5.34 vs     5.93</p>
<p>    Minority loss			 0.45 vs     0.45</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain		  0.28 vs     2.68 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Hour Glass Ltd runs a chain of watch shops in Singapore.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
